---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

import { zones, rulesForZone, networkEvidence, type Zone } from "../../../data/network";
import { getSystem } from "../../../data/model";
export function getStaticPaths(){return zones.map(zone=>({params:{slug:zone.slug},props:{zone}}));}
interface Props {zone:Zone}
const {zone}=Astro.props;
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const rules=rulesForZone(zone.slug);
const isVpn=zone.slug==="vpn_remote";
const isClient=zone.slug==="client";
const zoneCopy:Record<string,string[]>={"wan":["wan","vtnet0","Upstream DHCP; recorded 192.168.178.71","No local WAN DHCP scope","Nova Corp needs an upstream path for Internet access and the remote VPN listener. WAN is the firewall’s outside interface, not the company’s management VLAN.","An external VPN packet can reach the WAN listener on UDP 51820; it must still authenticate as a WireGuard peer. The upstream router’s port forwarding is separate from pfSense NAT.","Outside router / remote peer","Incoming UDP 51820","WireGuard peer authentication","wireguard-handshake"],"lan":["lan","vtnet1","10.99.99.1/24","10.99.99.100–10.99.99.199","The original untagged LAN is retained in the lab alongside the newer tagged networks. Do not treat it as one of the five VLANs.","The two broad default allows cover IPv4 and IPv6. A configured IPv6 rule is not proof of working IPv6 routing.","Legacy LAN device","Broad saved allow","Other networks via firewall",""],"mgmt":["opt1","vtnet1.10 · VLAN 10","10.10.10.1/24","10.10.10.100–10.10.10.199","IT needs a distinct administration area. The firewall has a management interface here; Proxmox management is still on the upstream network.","Two broad management permits remain. CLIENT has separate incoming rules that block management access. Full privileged management-plane isolation remains the next security gate.","Authorized management device (illustrative)","MGMT rule evaluation","Management interface","firewall-management-exposure"],"infra":["opt2","vtnet1.20 · VLAN 20","10.10.20.1/24","10.10.20.100–10.10.20.199","The company’s domain controllers and file server live on this infrastructure network so staff can reach shared services through the firewall.","DC01 is 10.10.20.10, DC02 is 10.10.20.11 and FILES01 is 10.10.20.20. The saved INFRA IPv4 rule is broad; same-VLAN traffic need not traverse pfSense.","NOVA-CLIENT on VLAN 40","Routed permitted traffic","DC01 / DC02 / FILES01","fileserver-subnet"],"app":["opt3","vtnet1.30 · VLAN 30","10.10.30.1/24","10.10.30.100–10.10.30.199","A reserved network allows Nova Corp to place future application workloads in a distinct segment. No deployed application server is confirmed in the Phase 2 inventory.","The saved IPv4 pass-to-any rule is permissive. Further restrictions and application validation are future work.","Future application (planned)","Configured broad allow","Other destinations",""],"client":["opt4","vtnet1.40 · VLAN 40","10.10.40.1/24","10.10.40.100–10.10.40.199","Employees need access to company services, not administrative tools. NOVA-CLIENT is the workstation used to test that distinction.","The first two CLIENT rules block firewall web management and the MGMT network. The next broadly permits other IPv4 traffic. The validation exercise retested DNS, AD, SMB and Internet access after correcting the management exposure.","NOVA-CLIENT 10.10.40.100","Two blocks, then remaining allow","Allowed business services","firewall-management-exposure"],"dmz":["opt5","vtnet1.50 · VLAN 50","10.10.50.1/24","10.10.50.100–10.10.50.199","Nova Corp reserved this area for later externally exposed application workloads. No deployed public-facing server is confirmed.","The current IPv4 rule broadly permits traffic from DMZ. Tighter security policy and public-service validation have not been implemented.","Future public workload (planned)","Configured broad allow","Other destinations",""],"vpn_remote":["opt6","tun_wg0 · WireGuard","10.10.60.1/24","No DHCP; configured peer 10.10.60.10/32","A remote laptop can use a separate encrypted network to reach selected company services. VPN_REMOTE is not an 802.1Q VLAN.","Four pass rules allow gateway ping and selected DC TCP/UDP/ICMP traffic. Two blocks restrict other INFRA and protected networks. Independent external-laptop validation is deferred.","Remote laptop (configured peer)","WireGuard + ordered VPN rules","Selected DC services","wireguard-handshake"]};
const [iface,device,ip,dhcp,purpose,behavior,origin,path,destination,incident]=zoneCopy[zone.slug];
---
<BaseLayout title={zone.name+" network"} description={"Explore the actual "+zone.name+" network, its connected systems and ordered firewall rules."} breadcrumbs={[{label:"Network",href:"network/"},{label:zone.name}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
 <div class="eyebrow">{zone.kind} / Network area</div><h1>{zone.name}</h1><p class="lead" style="margin-top:17px">{zone.purpose}</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main"><div>
  <section class="content-section"><h2>What is the {zone.name} network?</h2><p>{purpose}</p><h2 style="margin-top:24px">Why does Nova Corp use it?</h2><p>{behavior}</p><figure class="zone-flow"><div class="zone-flow-track"><div><strong>{origin}</strong></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><a href={base+"systems/nova-fw01/"}>{path}</a><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div>{destination}</div></div><figcaption>Illustrative request path. The saved rule order determines the action; this is not a new packet trace.</figcaption></figure>{isClient&&<p><a href={base+"network/rules/1795199640/"}>Blocked management web ports</a> · <a href={base+"network/rules/1795195682/"}>Blocked MGMT network</a></p>}{incident&&<p><a href={base+"incidents/"+incident+"/"}>Read the related investigation →</a></p>}</section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Firewall rules on this incoming interface</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:13px 0 18px">Rules are displayed in their documented order for this interface. A rule's configured action is not a live packet log; earlier blocks may override a broader later allow.</p>
    <ol class="rule-stack">{rules.map(rule=><li class="rule-step">
      <a href={base+"network/rules/"+rule.id+"/"} class="rule-entry">
        <span class={"rule-action "+(rule.action==="BLOCK"?"block":"pass")}>{rule.action}</span>
        <span><strong>{rule.description}</strong><small>{rule.protocol} · {rule.destination} · {rule.ports}</small></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a></li>)}</ol>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
   <h2>Which systems are related?</h2>
   <div class="card-list">{zone.devices.map(id=>{const system=getSystem(id);return system?<a class="system-card" href={base+"systems/"+system.slug+"/"}><small>{system.category}</small><h3>{system.name}</h3><p>{system.summary}</p><span class="readmore">Open system →</span></a>:null})}</div>
  </section>
  {isClient&&<section class="content-section"><div class="paper panel"><h2>Follow an employee request</h2><p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 18px">The workstation enters CLIENT. Two ordered rules block access to pfSense web management and the management network, followed by an allow for other traffic. The management-denial validation also preserved required business services.</p><a class="btn small" href={base+"network/rules/1795199640/"}>Start with the first block →</a><p style="margin-top:15px"><a href={base+"files/"}>Then follow a permitted company file request →</a></p></div></section>}
  {isVpn&&<div class="note warning"><strong>Remote access is not the same as a VLAN.</strong> This is a WireGuard tunnel with explicit DC-service permissions. Outside-network validation and privileged-admin access remain deferred; the saved rule configuration does not constitute an external end-to-end PASS.</div>}
  <section class="content-section"><details><summary>Technical checks</summary><p><strong>Where:</strong> pfSense shell.</p><h3>Check the interface</h3><pre><code>{"ifconfig "+device.split(" ")[0]}</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> {ip}; compare interface settings and the saved inventory.</p><h3>Inspect active firewall rules</h3><pre><code>pfctl -sr</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> the intended rules for this interface appear in the configured order. Review actual traffic separately.</p>{isClient&&<><h3>Confirm business traffic</h3><p><strong>Where:</strong> NOVA-CLIENT.</p><pre><code>Test-NetConnection 10.10.20.20 -Port 445</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> TcpTestSucceeded: True.</p></>}</details></section><section class="content-section"><h2>Engineering journals</h2><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/network/zones/"+zone.slug.toUpperCase()+"/"}>Complete network-zone documentation →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/network/DHCP/"}>Address assignment and DHCP →</a></p><p><a href={base+"journals/change_request_cr002/"}>Network installation journal →</a></p></section>
 </div><aside>
   <div class="sidebox"><h3>Zone profile</h3><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Kind</dt><dd>{zone.kind}</dd></div><div><dt>Interface</dt><dd>{iface}</dd></div><div><dt>Device</dt><dd>{device}</dd></div><div><dt>Address assignment</dt><dd>{dhcp}</dd></div><div><dt>Documented subnet</dt><dd>{zone.address}</dd></div><div><dt>Gateway</dt><dd>{zone.gateway}</dd></div><div><dt>Explicit rules</dt><dd>{rules.length}</dd></div></dl></div>
   <div class="sidebox"><h3>Source</h3><p class="muted">Saved rule configuration and previous specific connection tests are distinct kinds of evidence.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={networkEvidence.zone(zone.slug)}>Open network profile ↗</a></div>
   <div class="sidebox"><a href={base+"network/"}>← All network areas</a><p style="margin-top:12px"><a href={base+"network/rules/"}>All firewall rules →</a></p></div>
 </aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.zone-flow{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--rule);padding:18px;border-radius:12px;margin:24px 0}.zone-flow-track{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}.zone-flow-track>div,.zone-flow-track>a{flex:1;min-width:0;text-align:center;padding:12px 8px;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);overflow-wrap:anywhere}.zone-flow-track>span{color:var(--c-amber);animation:zoneflow 2s ease-in-out infinite}.zone-flow figcaption{text-align:center;font-size:.84rem;margin-top:12px;color:var(--ink)}@keyframes zoneflow{50%{transform:translateX(3px);opacity:.6}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.zone-flow-track>span{animation:none}}@media(max-width:600px){.zone-flow-track{flex-direction:column}.zone-flow-track>span{transform:rotate(90deg);animation:none}.zone-flow-track>div,.zone-flow-track>a{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}}</style>
